# November 19, 2026: Harford County, Maryland, region md, drawn at random by tools/choose.py (the county was then drawn
# at random from Maryland's counties other than Frederick, which md_vdxv had worked). Nothing was on the map in Harford County.
# Facts come from sources opened in this session: Wikipedia read as raw text (wiki_raw.py, the county's Register list with
# --rows), Maryland DNR park pages and the DNR walking-tour PDF for the Rock Run Historic Area, HMdb marker pages (Maryland
# State Parks' own signs at Rock Run, Lapidum, Deer Creek and Stafford), the National Park Service, the Friends of Jerusalem
# Mill, the Concord Point Lighthouse and Lock House museums, Ladew Gardens, Baltimore Yearly Meeting, the Historical Society
# of Harford County, a Harford County press release and the Archdiocese of Baltimore's Catholic Review, all read with
# tools/page.py. Brick values come from what the sources say a place is built of, or from a picture opened with
# tools/brick.py look ('Jerusalem Mills Village-Jerusalem Mill HDR, August 2012.jpg': stone ground storey, red-painted board
# siding above and one red brick chimney, so 'some'); '?' where nothing opened settled it.
